</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Anderson</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Modeling survival and testing biological hypotheses using marked animals: a unified approach with case studies</article-title><source>Ecol Monogr</source><year>1992</year><volume>62</volume><fpage>67</fpage><lpage>118</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2307/2937171</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fowler</surname><given-names>CW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Density dependence as related to life history strategy</article-title><source>Ecology</source><year>1981</year><volume>62</volume><fpage>602</fpage><lpage>610</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2307/1937727</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Owen-Smith</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Demographic determination of the shape of density dependence for three African ungulate populations</article-title><source>Ecol Monogr</source><year>2006</year><volume>76</volume><fpage>93</fpage><lpage>109</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wolff</surname><given-names>JO</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Population regulation in mammals: an evolutionary perspective</article-title><source>J Anim Ecol</source><year>1997</year><volume>66</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>13</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2307/5959</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bowen</surname><given-names>WD</given-names></name><name><surname>McMillan</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Mohn</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group>